# Three players: Mardu Siegebreaker's "for each opponent, create a tapped token that's a copy of the exiled card attacking that
# opponent" is one instruction, so its two Ornithopter tokens - one attacking Bot2, one attacking Bot3 - are created together in
# one event (CR 101.4), and Mister Fantastic, Reed Richards' "Whenever one or more tokens you control enter" triggers once for
# them, not once for each opponent (CR 603.2c). Each token is attacking its own opponent (CR 508.4).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mister Fantastic, Reed Richards
Ornithopter
Mardu Siegebreaker
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mister Fantastic, Reed Richards.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mardu Siegebreaker.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T7 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Mardu Siegebreaker > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Stack = Mister Fantastic, Reed Richards
? Stack.Count = 1

[Expect]
Combat.Attackers = Mardu Siegebreaker > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot3
